# 0163: a MovementZone=CrusherAll unit (the Battle Fortress) drives through every wall, not just the Crushable= ones.
#
# UnitClass Per_Cell_Process (FUN_0073AFD4) flattens an overlay whose type says Crushable=yes for any
# Crusher, and also flattens Wall=yes overlays when the unit's MovementZone is CrusherAll (the test is
# the zone id 0xC at 0x0073B02D; read from the reverse-engineered description in
# github.com/YuriPlanet/vera20k, src/sim/movement/bump_crush.rs, read only; in stock rules the Battle
# Fortress alone, which is also our OmniCrusher= unit). We only knew the Crushable= walls (patch P4),
# so a Battle Fortress treated Allied/Soviet base walls as solid and went round them or shot them.
# Cells with a wall that is not Crushable= are marked state 3 in World::crush_wall_ ("standing, CrusherAll
# only"); crush_grid_of/crush_leak_of hand an OmniCrusher unit the grid that opens them, step_wall_crush
# flattens them for it only, and repath uses the same grid. Plain Crushers keep the old grid. Not a World
# member, so the save format is unchanged (the derived grid is a function-local cache).

